## Start

```bash
just init
just run
```

The dummy application prints `Hello, Scala!` after compiling successfully.

## Validation

```bash
just ci
```

`just ci` runs Scalafmt, built-in and project-local Scalafix rules, strict scalac checks, WartRemover, Find Security Bugs, dependency declaration and lock checks, codespell, Semgrep, MUnit, Scalafix testkit, ArchUnit, scoverage, Trivy, and sbt-updates. A failure from any tool stops the pipeline.

Useful focused commands:

- `just code-style`
- `just code-scalafix`
- `just code-typecheck`
- `just code-warts`
- `just code-security`
- `just code-deptry`
- `just code-semgrep`
- `just code-architecture`
- `just code-audit`
- `just test`
- `just test-coverage`

## Architecture

Production code is split into three packages:

```text
cli -> application -> domain
```

ArchUnit enforces dependency direction and cycle freedom. The local Scalafix build under `scalafix/` implements and tests semantic source rules before those rules analyze the application.

